}"}

{"explanation":"Copy the input with slice() so the original array is never mutated, then sort the copy with a numeric comparator (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0) instead of the default lexicographic sort or a subtraction that could misbehave with Infinity. For odd length, return the middle element. For even length, return the mean of the two middle elements, computed as lo + (hi - lo) / 2 to avoid overflow from adding two very large values. If both middle values are the same infinity, hi - lo would be NaN, so that case returns lo directly. The array is assumed nonempty and numeric, as specified.","code":"function solve(arr) {
  const s = arr.slice().sort((a, b) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0));
  const n = s.length;
  const mid = Math.floor(n / 2);
  if (n % 2 === 1) return s[mid];
  const lo = s[mid - 1];
  const hi = s[mid];
  if (lo === hi) return lo;
  return lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
}"}

