{"explanation":"solve takes a value and returns a new HTML-escaped string without mutating the input. Non-string input is converted with String (null/undefined become empty string). A single regex replace with a lookup map handles all five characters in one pass, so ampersands are never double-escaped (e.g. '<' becomes '&lt;' and the '&' in that output is not re-escaped).","code":"function solve(input) {
  if (input === null || input === undefined) return '';
  const map = {
    '&': '&amp;',
    '<': '&lt;',
    '>': '&gt;',
    '"': '&quot;',
    "'": '&#39;'
  };
  return String(input).replace(/[&<>"']/g, function (ch) {
