{"explanation":"Return [] for an empty matrix (or one whose rows are empty, since a 0-column matrix has no rows to transpose into). Otherwise build a new array with one row per column index, filling each entry from the corresponding input row. New arrays are created and the input is only read, so nothing is mutated.","code":"function solve(matrix) {
  if (!Array.isArray(matrix) || matrix.length === 0) return [];
  const cols = matrix[0].length;
  const result = [];
  for (let j = 0; j < cols; j++) {
