{"explanation":"Standard base64 uses '+', '/' and '=' padding; base64url uses '-', '_' and omits padding. The function returns a new string via replace calls (strings are immutable, so the input is never mutated). '+' maps to '-', '/' maps to '_', and trailing '=' characters are stripped with a regex anchored at the end. Global regexes handle all occurrences.","code":"function solve(input) {
